---
Deploys a Git commit through its service, releases a prebuilt image, or rolls back

Usage: leptoskit deploy [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --verified-descriptor <VERIFIED_DESCRIPTOR>
          Packaging descriptor whose digest was independently authenticated
      --descriptor-sha256 <DESCRIPTOR_SHA256>
          Independently authenticated SHA-256 of the packaging descriptor
      --version <VERSION>
          Immutable image tag, or a Git commit for the connected deployment service
      --rollback <ROLLBACK>
          Previously recorded version to roll back to. Schema history must match
      --setup
          First deploy: prepare the server and boot Postgres and the tunnel
      --maintenance
          Stop the current app before a schema-changing release. On failure it stays stopped until an operator recovers the schema and application
      --recover
          Redeploy a recorded version after recovery without reusing it as a new release
      --rollback-schema
          Stop writers and run checked down migrations to the rollback target
      --yes
          Confirm an explicitly requested database rollback
  -h, --help
          Print help
